  "body": "**Replaces #364**, which was opened from the old fork. GitHub detached that fork from this repo's network when NeoTech/Camcraft was briefly private, so #364 can no longer be updated. This branch carries the merge with main at #461. The conflicts were the MCP module/import lists (#180's pick/area/features and this PR's render), all kept. After the merge: `mcp_render` 5/5, `mcp` 9/9, clippy clean.\n\n## What changed\n- **New MCP tool `render_stock`.** It runs the post gate's own program simulation (`stock_sim::simulate_document`) and paints what stands by deviation class: clean, rest, gouge, unjudged.\n  - **CPU rasteriser.** It draws the result with a new rasteriser (`crates/app/src/raster.rs`): flat-shaded triangles through a depth buffer, orthographic camera, PNG via the `png` crate. No GPU.\n  - **Answer.** The PNG comes back as an MCP image content block (`{\"type\":\"image\",\"data\":…,\"mimeType\":\"image/png\"}`) after the text block. Alongside it, a JSON summary gives:\n    - rest and gouge cell counts, volume, maximum and where it is;\n    - the rest's top bounds and the drawn stock's bounds;\n    - judged-cell count and image facts.\n  - **Arguments:** `width`/`height` (16–2048, default 640×480), `view` (`iso` | `top`), `toolpath` (bool: feed, plunge and rapid moves drawn over the stock).\n  - **Refusals, each named:** no simulation (no stock or nothing generated), no material standing above the stock floor, bad or unknown arguments. Unsupported programs (5-axis, rotary, lathe) refuse with the sim's own reason, as the post gate does.\n- `mcp/mod.rs` `tool_ok` lifts the PNG out of the JSON into the image block, so neither the text nor `structuredContent` carries the base64.\n- `mcp/tools.rs` gets one table row only. **Note:** PR #314 also adds a row to this table, so a one-line conflict is possible and trivial to resolve.\n- **Dependency:** `png = \"0.18\"` is now a direct dependency of `camcraft-app`, declared in the workspace. It was already in `Cargo.lock` through `image`, so no new crate enters the tree (MIT/Apache-2.0). base64 is hand-written (a few lines) rather than a new crate.\n- `docs/decisions/182-mcp-sim-render.md`\n\n## How tested\n- New `crates/app/tests/mcp_render.rs` (5 tests):\n  - Uncut job: the PNG decodes at the requested size, stock covers the frame, rest volume is 8000 (40×40×5), and the base64 is not in the JSON.\n  - The same session gives the same bytes twice, and a fresh session gives the same bytes too.\n  - The top view with the toolpath overlay contains the feed-move colour.\n  - `render_stock_shows_what_the_program_cut`: Face 2 mm down changes the bytes, the stock top goes to z 18 and rest to 4800. Facing down to the part top takes rest to 0 and removes every amber pixel (more than 10% of the frame repaints).\n  - `render_stock_refuses_when_no_material_stands`: facing below the stock floor refuses by name, where it used to draw a flat sheet under the block.\n  - The tool is listed with its schema, and every argument refusal is named.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_render --test mcp`: 9 passed. `clippy -D warnings` is clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` fell back to batch because Cargo.toml changed. The only failures also fail on `upstream/main` c442118 on this machine:\n  - `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag` (version pin; PR #345)\n  - `swarf_pose_continuity` ×2 (PR #351)\n  - the headless-GPU ui tests (no adapter here)\n  - the two macOS pixel-snapshot diffs (#255 / PR #359)\n\n## Not exercised\n- Not tried from a real MCP client (Claude Desktop etc.). Only the JSON-RPC tool path is tested.\n\nChangelog: MCP `render_stock` returns a PNG of the simulated stock (by deviation class, optional toolpath overlay) with rest and gouge volume and bounds (#182)\n\nFixes #182\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
